# DVD Tivat - browser configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the two values from the Supabase
# dashboard: Project Settings -> API. `.env.local` is git-ignored; this file is
# tracked and must keep placeholders only.
#
#   Project URL     -> VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   Publishable key -> VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   (starts with sb_publishable_)
#
# The publishable key is PUBLIC by design. It is compiled into the browser
# bundle of every Supabase application and grants nothing on its own: the
# anonymous database role holds no table privilege and no executable function in
# this schema.
#
# The SECRET key (sb_secret_...) is a different thing and must NEVER appear:
# not here, not in `.env.local`, not in any variable whose name starts with
# VITE_ (Vite inlines those into the bundle, so a secret in one is published to
# every visitor), and not in any tracked file. Nothing this application does
# needs it. If a feature seems to require the secret key inside the app itself,
# that is a design smell to raise, not a requirement to satisfy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
